The attached image demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the expression of costimulatory molecules on dendritic cells (DCs), a key aspect of its adjuvant activity. Bone marrow-derived DCs incubated with Nano-11 (black line) exhibited a marked increase in the surface expression of CD80 and CD86 compared to medium-treated control cells (gray line), indicated by a significant rightward shift in the histograms. A slight increase in CD40 expression was also observed. This finding, referenced in Section 3.4 of the PDF, supports that Nano-11 activates DCs, promoting their maturation and capacity to present antigens and initiate robust immune responses.